# 🛠 Structure of a Go Program

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Hello, Go!")
}
```

---

## Explanation

### package main

Defines the main package.

### import "fmt"

Imports the formatting package used for input and output.

### func main()

The entry point of every Go program.

### fmt.Println()

Prints output to the console.

---

# 🚀 First Go Program

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Welcome to Golang!")
}
```

### Output

```
Welcome to Golang!
```

